<title>USA: Sioux Falls hogs off $1.25-1.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sioux Falls hogs off $1.25-1.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said barrows and gilts were $1.25 to $1.50 lower. Trading was slow. Top $56.25 per cwt.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    220-260 lbs    55.50-56.25, mostly 56.00</p>
<p>		  260-270 lbs    55.00-55.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-280 lbs    54.00-55.00</p>
<p>		  280-290 lbs    53.00-54.00</p>
<p>    US 3-4    290-300 lbs    52.00-53.00</p>
<p>Sows - steady/up $3.50. Top $59.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-3     300-450 lbs   45.75-49.00,</p>
<p>		   Most 300-350 lbs 45.75-46.00</p>
<p>		   450-500 lbs   51.00-52.00</p>
<p>		   500-650 lbs   55.00-57.00,</p>
<p>		   Some 600-650 lbs 59.00</p>
</text>
